{
  "esm": "0.4.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "divergence_duo_pde",
    "description": "Flux-form divergence d(div)/dt = div(F, dim=cell) on a DUO icosahedral triangular mesh. F is the edge-normal flux (edge-located, shape [n_edges]); div is the cell-centered output. The divergence is lowered from divergence_duo (Heikes et al. 2023; the triangular-primal analogue of Skamarock et al. 2012, Eq. 24): sum_k edge_sign_on_face[i,k] * dc_edge[e]/area[i] * F[e], e = edges_on_face[i,k]. MMS edge fluxes are injected at bind time by the unstructured-divergence Layer-B runner; the F tendency is frozen (zero) so one RHS evaluation yields the discrete divergence of the prescribed flux field."
  },
  "models": {
    "M": {
      "grid": "domain",
      "variables": {
        "div": { "type": "state", "shape": ["n_cells"], "location": "cell_center", "default": 0.0 },
        "F":   { "type": "state", "shape": ["n_edges"], "location": "edge_normal", "default": 0.0 }
      },
      "equations": [
        { "lhs": { "op": "D", "args": ["div"], "wrt": "t" }, "rhs": { "op": "div", "args": ["F"], "dim": "cell" } },
        { "lhs": { "op": "D", "args": ["F"], "wrt": "t" }, "rhs": 0.0 }
      ],
      "time": { "t0": 0.0, "t_final": 0.001 }
    }
  }
}
